  "notes": {
    "identity": "siteId, gatewayId and deviceId are claimed routing codes. When provided, gatewaySerial and deviceSerial identify physical hardware and must be sent together.",
    "legacyCompatibility": "Schema 1.1 without serials works for both bound telemetry and new discovery. An unbound no-serial route creates a separate claimed-ID candidate and is never merged into a serial-keyed candidate.",
    "multiDeviceGateway": "SMARTLOGGER-001 and SPM91-01 belong to one gateway candidate because their payloads share gatewaySerial GW-SN-A1B2C3D4. Their different deviceSerial values keep the devices distinct, and both enter normal ingestion after pairing and config activation.",
    "lotNumber": "Unsigned 32-bit running number. Retry of the same logical message must retain the same lotNumber.",
    "pm2230": "Values and canonical fields are examples. Use a verified Schneider PM2230 register map for addresses, scaling and data types.",
    "energy": "Canonical energy values are normalized to Wh/varh before publishing.",
    "firstContact": "Anonymous first contact receives no dataAcept and creates no production sample. In demo-anonymous mode, admin pairing activates the exact approved site/gateway/device routes immediately; a syntactically valid Client ID and blank username/password may be used without a credential reconnect.",
    "security": "demo-anonymous is for controlled demonstrations only. Any anonymous client with a syntactically valid Client ID can subscribe to every topic and wildcard and publish to any full telemetry topic; ingestion still requires matching topic/payload identities and an approved binding before persistence. Control and non-telemetry publishing remain restricted. Set GATEWAY_AUTH_MODE=credential for production provisioning and per-gateway credentials.",
    "register": "The /register topic is not used. Discovery occurs on the telemetry topic only."
  }
